{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>For the pace of the work.</b> An expression of acquisition and property." "<b>Until I come to my lord at Seir.</b> After I settle my children, my wives, and my flocks in their resting place, I will come to you at Seir to be honored, and there we shall see each other in joy and peace."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The Hebrew רגל is here interpreted as related to רגיל/הרגילות in the sense of customary dealing; the bracketed note glosses it as a term of purchase and property."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:15.818934851Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}